    end_the_sequence}. The vault aim hangs off the network aim rather than
    sitting in the chain, because the vault is optional lore and must never gate
    the conclusion.

    Aim `status: "locked"` is presentation only -- objectives-manager.js:412 and
    :543 auto-reveal a locked parent aim when one of its tasks completes -- so a
    locked aim can never strand a task. Every task therefore ships `active`.

    Anything a player can legitimately walk past (Morrison, Elena, Park, the
    vault, the lore drops) is `optional: true`, so aim completion never depends
    on content the player was allowed to skip.

